From a9931f431e4cf39490595eb32273399711ee2ea1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: gavin_darkglider <rbrown4014@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 22:14:10 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 02/13] core: fix bugs found while reviving the code base

- libfbsplash: pass the fifo command to fputs() instead of using it as a
  format string.
- libfbsplashrender: fbsplashr_tty_silent_cleanup() did c_lflag &=
  (ICANON|ECHO), clearing every other local mode flag of the tty on exit;
  check mmap() against MAP_FAILED; don't closedir(NULL) or fscanf() a
  NULL FILE when the input class can't be read; tty fd checks used !fd;
  off-by-one in fbsplashr_tty_silent_set().
- effects: the background fade child returned instead of exiting in 8bpp
  modes, leaving a second copy of the caller running.
- render: box opacity was forced to 0xff by a leftover ', 1', so
  blendin()/blendout() never faded boxes.
- image: '!a & b' precedence bug decided whether to add an alpha channel;
  is_png() looked at an uninitialized header for files < 8 bytes.
- ttf: rewrite the UTF-8 decoder, which read past the end of truncated
  sequences and silently truncated non-BMP characters; use ceilf()
  instead of a private ceil() (that rounded) in the kernel helper.
- daemon: bound the %s in the /proc/*/stat scan; check read()/chdir().
- Use proper #if blocks for WANT_TTF/WANT_MNG ('defined' inside a macro
  expansion is undefined behaviour) and PATH_SYS/PATH_PROC.
- Missing declarations/headers (makedev, mount, list_ringadd,
  obj_visibility_set) that GCC 14 rejects; make arg_task static so the
  unified fbsplashctl links with -fno-common (GCC 10+ default).
- fbcondecor_ctl: return a failure exit status when an operation fails,
  and say why setpic is refused for an inactive console.
- Uninitialized buffers when fgets()/fscanf() fail.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_013zuE5eXGVUDWEu4YZj7gYa
